{
 "title": "Linearised explicit formula for prime patterns: frozen holdout test",
 "frozen_on": "2026-11-25",
 "discovery_range": "x <= 2e9 (pairs, triples, Sophie Germain pairs); prime sums (regressors) to 4e9",
 "holdout_range": "x in (2e9, 2e10]; pair statistics computed on (2e9, 2e10], prime sums on (4e9, 4e10]",
 "statistic": "Y(u) = (sum_{p<=x, pattern} prod ln(L_i(p)) - S x)/sqrt(x) on the grid u = ln X_k, X_k = floor(exp(k/2048)); regressors (theta(a x) - a x)/sqrt(x) and theta(a x, chi)/sqrt(x) for primitive chi of conductor <= 30; fit: differences of the series weighted by (ln x)^(-k/2), FFT (rectangular window), bins with 2 <= gamma <= 6000 (and 2..300), weighted least squares on real and imaginary parts with nuisance regressors (u, u^2, exp(-u/2), exp(-u), constant drift); noise variance per bin from the smoothed squared residuals (41 bins, 3 passes); errors from (X^T W X)^-1. Model 'all': zeta coefficient(s) free, one loudness factor for all predicted characters together, free coefficients for the null set 3.1, 4.1, 5.2, 7.1, 7.4, 8.1, 8.2, 11.1, 12.1, 9.1 (those not predicted present). Model 'cond': one loudness per conductor.",
 "conjecture": "sum_{n<=x} prod_i Lambda(a_i n + b_i) = S x + S sum_i (1/a_i)[(psi(a_i x) - a_i x) + sum_{chi primitive} c_i(chi) psi(a_i x, chi)] + (terms not linear in the zeros), c_i(chi) = mean of conj(chi(a_i n + b_i)) over the admissible n mod cond(chi). Pairs (n, n+h): zeta coefficient 2 S(h); chi enters with 2 S(h) mu(q) conj(chi(h)) / prod_{p|q}(p-2) iff chi is even with odd squarefree conductor q coprime to h, else 0.",
